NAME
    help - list all available commands with one-line summaries

SYNOPSIS
    help

DESCRIPTION
    Prints every registered builtin, module command, shipped program,
    and language construct, one per line, with a brief usage summary.
    Any arguments are ignored.

    To read the full manual page for a single command, use man(1).

EXAMPLES
    help
    help | grep trace

EXIT STATUS
    0   Always succeeds.

SEE ALSO
    man(1), which(1), command(1)
